# Elastic Crawler Control - Config Generator Feature

## Git Workflow

This is a fork of `ugosan/elastic-crawler-control` with a feature branch for the config generator.

- **Branch**: `feature/config-generator`
- **Upstream**: `ugosan/elastic-crawler-control`
- **Goal**: Contribute config generator back to upstream when ready

```bash
# Sync with upstream
git fetch upstream
git checkout main && git pull upstream main
git checkout feature/config-generator && git rebase main
```

## Task Planning: Beads (bd)

This project uses **Beads** (`bd`) for task planning and issue tracking.

### Essential Commands

```bash
bd ready                    # See unblocked work
bd list                     # List all issues
bd create "Title" --description "..."  # Create task
bd close <issue-id>         # Close task
bd show <issue-id>          # View details
```

### Linking Issues to Specs
```bash
bd create "Task" --labels "spec:config-generation"
bd list --label spec:orchestration
```

## Project Structure

```
elastic-crawler-control/
├── crawler-service/app/     # Backend (FastAPI + Agno agents)
│   ├── agents/              # Agno-powered agents and workflow
│   ├── routes/              # API endpoints
│   └── utils/               # Shared utilities
├── frontend/src/            # React + Elastic UI
├── knowledge/               # Extraction patterns, Agno guide
├── openspec/                # Feature specifications
├── docs/                    # Workflow documentation
└── .beads/                  # Issue tracking
```

## Key Reminders

- Always check `bd ready` at start of work session
- Use `python-dotenv` with `override=True` for env vars
- No mocking - use real services (Open Crawler, Elasticsearch)
- Code should be modular, small files, well-documented
- **Read `knowledge/agno/workflow-guide.md`** before modifying agent code
